# Progress in Stylistics: Theory, Statistics, Computers.

**Authors:** Milic, Louis

## Abstract
Assesses the progress made in computational stylistics over the past 25 years. Discusses theoretical notions of style. Describes certain trends that emerge from relevant articles in conference proceedings and academic journals. Concludes there has been progress in the accumulation of data, the creation of databases and archives, and construction of software but not substance. (DK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ452249

